/**
 * Validate that a moderator can retrieve all poll votes for a specific poll,
 * using search and pagination features.
 *
 * This end-to-end scenario covers the full business workflow of poll voting
 * analytics and moderation review, as required for forum/poll compliance use
 * cases, and demonstrates that role-based access is correctly respected. The
 * flow also checks that data returned respects filtering by poll ID and that
 * unauthorized roles are blocked from accessing the moderation endpoint.
 *
 * Steps:
 *
 * 1. Register a discussion board member (using a random id and current time).
 * 2. Create a discussion thread as the registered member, specifying required
 *    thread/category info and timestamps.
 * 3. Create a poll attached to that thread (using member context), with a
 *    configurable prompt/question and multi/single select enabled, set to
 *    expire in the future.
 * 4. Simulate multiple members and have them submit poll votes (on the poll
 *    created), so there are several votes to be listed. Ensure votes have
 *    different selected_options to cover search features.
 * 5. Assign moderator role to a member via admin endpoint.
 * 6. From the perspective of this moderator, use the moderator endpoint to fetch
 *    all poll votes for the created poll (using search body with
 *    discussionboard_poll_id filter and reasonable pagination params) and
 *    verify:
 *
 *    - All votes for this poll appear (IDs and options match those submitted).
 *    - Pagination/limit fields are included, and data completeness is maintained.
 *    - Filtering by selected_option or voting_member_id works as expected.
 *    - Only a moderator can successfully access this endpoint; a normal member
 *         attempting this should see a permission error.
